Z||000005||Black88GT||12-13-2000||03:29 PM||||Hell yeah! I love Office Space!!<P>"I come in every morning late, I sneak in the back door so the boss doesn't see me, then I ... space out for an hour"<P>"Space out?"<P>"Yeah its where I sit at my desk and stare at the computer to make it look like I'm working....I'd say in a week I do about 5 hours of work"<P><BR>haha its great....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||12-13-2000||04:30 PM||||I remember once when a young girl, maybe 6 years old came to me and asked "What is the rain?"...I looked at her and replied "Rain is when God is crying". The little girl thought for a moment, then looked at me sadly and said "Why is God crying?"... I looked at her, put my hand on her small shoulder, and replied "Probobly because of something you did!"....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||12-13-2000||04:54 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>I remember once when a young girl, maybe 6 years old came to me and asked "What is the rain?"...I looked at her and replied "Rain is when God is crying". The little girl thought for a moment, then looked at me sadly and said "Why is God crying?"... I looked at her, put my hand on her small shoulder, and replied "Probobly because of something you did!"....    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I really hated it when adults told me cr@p like that when I was little.. I was smart enough to know it wasn't true, yet not ONE person (teachers, etc..) would tell me the truth.. so I went to the library and got a book on weather, and learned it on my own.<BR>I was wondering about thunderstorms and not rain though, but I was younger than 6.... just in case you were wondering, I was reading fluently by the time I was 5... and by the end of grade 1, I was reading Hardy Boys novels on my own.. (they're not *all* about smugglers, honest! hehehe) so a kids weather book was a piece of cake when I was 4.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I do remember that I got mad at a babysitter when she took that book away from me, and said I couldn't read it... she didn't think I could read or something like that..<P>funny story though, I would have loved to have seen the look on that kid's face.. LOL...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-13-2000).]||||reg||8
